# --- What is excluded from the public repository ---
#
# The rule, stated as it actually is. Two things ship: every SOURCE file the
# pipeline needs, so a clean checkout can rebuild the whole study from scratch,
# AND the study's own generated data and figures (05_solution/*.csv, the plots,
# the drawing sheets, the link-preview card, the consolidated report), so the
# repository can be read without running anything. What is excluded is only the
# REPORT BUILD's intermediates -- case.docx, the rendered equation images and
# the two component PDFs, all of which are rebuilt from the same outputs on
# every run -- plus Python caches.
#
# This header used to claim "every GENERATED artifact is excluded, except the
# one consolidated report", which described a repository this has never been:
# 135 generated CSVs, PNGs and the solver config under 01_..08_ are tracked,
# deliberately, and so are the two link-preview images under assets/.
#
# Previously 07_report/, run_all.py, draw_engineering.py and 00_overview/ were
# all excluded while the artifacts they produce were published. That shipped a
# repository which could not rebuild its own headline deliverable, and left
# README.md, requirements.txt and check_claims.py referring to files a clone
# did not contain.

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Generated by 07_report/build_docx.py on every run (LaTeX-rendered equations)
07_report/_equations/

# Generated documents. case.docx is written to both 07_report/ and the project
# root; this basename rule excludes both copies.
case.docx

# Exclude all PDFs from the project tree -- the plots album and the data
# dossier are intermediate products of the report build...
*.pdf
# ...except the consolidated technical report, which is the deliverable.
!aero_dynamic_stall_report.pdf

# NOTE: aero_style.py and project_meta.py are NOT excluded -- they are imported
# by 01_geometry, 02_mesh, 06_postprocessing, 07_report and the validation
# scripts, so the published pipeline cannot run without them.
